-- title:
--   Frozen rational global entropy data for the DWZ fourth-power candidate
-- statement:
--   Exact rational data for the global 45-cell coarse distribution in the Duan–Wu–Zhou fourth-power candidate at $q=5$. Cells are the triples $(i,j,k)$ of nonnegative integers with $i+j+k=8$, in the released order. The distribution $\alpha$ is rationalized first at denominator $10^{15}$, then exactly symmetrized in X and Y; its resulting common denominator is $2\cdot10^{15}$. The data also supply an independent strictly positive reference distribution $y$, an additive potential $g(i,j,k)=\lambda_0+\lambda_X(i)+\lambda_Y(j)+\lambda_Z(k)$, error allowance $\varepsilon=10^{-8}$, and the exact rational number
--
--   $$U=-\sum_{i+j+k=8}\alpha_{ijk}g(i,j,k)+\varepsilon.$$
--
--   The intended certified conclusion is $H(\rho)\le U$ for every probability distribution with the same three marginals as $\alpha$, using natural-log entropy. These are definitions, not assertions of positivity, normalization, logarithmic bounds, entropy optimality, or tensor extraction; those facts must be separately proved. The reference need not share the marginals of $\alpha$. Integer scales and rational log parameters are witnesses for the public exact-series log certificate. Retuning a component's region weights leaves this global distribution and global entropy certificate unchanged.
-- source:
--   Duan, Wu, Zhou, Faster Matrix Multiplication via Asymmetric Hashing, arXiv:2210.10173v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.10173v5, global Equation (25); released data https://osf.io/dta6p/, code/data/power4_dup_2.371919.mat SHA256 2aa5713eb352bc94c939d340743c4107b42d274c9fa2058ff879cd7603142aeb. Exact rational candidate preparation follows FixGlobal and the full VerifyGlobal entropy-loss sign; independent positive-reference dual witnesses were frozen, not trusted as optimizer output. These data do not assert complete feasibility or the bound omega<2.37193.

